ARTIFACT SUMMARY (parity with web features/dashboard/widgets/BackupMonitorWidget.tsx)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Registry: id `backup-monitor`, category `system`, default 2x2, min 1x2, max 4x40
  reproduced as BackupMonitorWidget.metadata (+ clamp()); asserted in tests.
- Data sources: bound through the shared state-holder layer (P1/S8) —
  BackupMonitorViewModel reads a StateHolderModel<LoadableState<[BackupRunVM]>>
  (the canonical AppContainer.loadable(from: adminStore.backupRuns(), map:) adapter);
  literal-state init for previews/tests. No direct HTTP in the view.
- Shared components reused: TSCard/TSGlassPanel/TSStatCard/TSMetricLabel (data-display+ui),
  TSBadge (ui), TSEmptyState/TSQueryError/TSSkeleton/TSStatSkeleton (feedback),
  typography + design tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius). WidgetShell is
  out-of-scope/unbuilt, so its chrome (title/icon, freshness, stale+offline chips,
  refresh, skeleton, error) is reproduced locally with existing primitives.
- States rendered: loading (skeleton), empty (TSEmptyState), error (TSQueryError+retry),
  stale (chip + refresh), offline (cached + offline chip). Layouts: compact (cols<=1),
  standard (2-3), wide (>=4, last-5 Recent Runs). All web `t()` keys mapped to P1/S10.
- a11y: composed VoiceOver label (title+relative time+status); refresh button labeled;
  reduce-motion honored by reused skeleton/components; accessibilityElement(.contain).
- Telemetry (P1/S11): emits `view.opened` (TelemetryEvent.ScreenView) with surface slug
  `BackupMonitorWidget` on appear via the injected WidgetTelemetry seam.
- Tests: decode adapter, ISO date parse, sort/latest/recent projection, status+tone
  mapping, byte/relative/duration formatting, registry metadata + clamp, a11y label
  composer, view-model state projection (loaded/empty/offline), telemetry view.opened
  emission, refresh callback, and per-state ImageRenderer render-smoke across 3 sizes.

