cmd: (cd apps/apple && DEVELOPER_DIR=.../Xcode xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync \
      -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16' build test)
Result: ** TEST FAILED **   IOS_EXIT=65
Root cause (test EXECUTION, not compilation — BLOCKED by runner infra):
  "TeslaSync encountered an error (Early unexpected exit, operation never finished
   bootstrapping ... Test crashed with signal kill before establishing connection.)"
  "IDETestOperationsObserverDebug: Failure collecting diagnostics from simulator:
   xcrun: error: unable to find utility 'simctl'"
Evidence of the true cause: the running CoreSimulator XPC service is the
CommandLineTools build, not Xcode's —
  PID 965 = /Library/Developer/PrivateFrameworks/CoreSimulator.framework/.../com.apple.CoreSimulator.CoreSimulatorService
The global active developer dir is CommandLineTools:
  `xcode-select -p` (no env) -> /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools
DEVELOPER_DIR redirects the client tools but NOT the launchd-vended CoreSimulatorService,
so Xcode 26.5's testmanagerd cannot establish a stable session with the CLT simulator
service (boot/erase/shutdown intermittently return SimError 405 / "server died").
Remediation requires `sudo xcode-select -s /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer`,
which is unavailable on this runner (`sudo: a password is required`).

